  "output": "Both analyses are complete. Here's the full performance audit:\n\n---\n\n## Performance Analysis: `cworkplace`\n\n---\n\n### 1. N+1 Query Patterns\n\n**Most critical: `notify()` creates notifications one-by-one**\n\n`apps/api/src/server/notify.ts:27`\n```typescript\n// ❌ N separate INSERT statements\nfor (const row of rows) await db.notification.create({ data: row });\n\n// ✅ One batch INSERT\nconst created = await db.notification.createManyAndReturn({ data: rows });\n```\n\n---\n\n**realtime-plugin.ts — loops with `await db.*` inside**\n\nEvery handler in `apps/api/src/server/plugins/realtime-plugin.ts` has this pattern:\n\n```typescript\n// ❌ Comment handler (lines 92–144): 50 comments → 50 post queries + 50 parent queries\nfor (const comment of rows) {\n  const post = await db.post.findUnique({ where: { id: comment.postId }, ... });\n  if (comment.parentId) {\n    const parent = await db.comment.findUnique({ where: { id: comment.parentId }, ... });\n  }\n}\n\n// ✅ Batch-fetch before the loop\nconst postIds = [...new Set(rows.map(c => c.postId))];\nconst posts = await db.post.findMany({ where: { id: { in: postIds } }, select: { ... } });\nconst postMap = new Map(posts.map(p => [p.id, p]));\n\nconst parentIds = rows.map(c => c.parentId).filter(Boolean);\nconst parents = await db.comment.findMany({ where: { id: { in: parentIds } }, select: { ... } });\nconst parentMap = new Map(parents.map(p => [p.id, p]));\n\nfor (const comment of rows) {\n  const post = postMap.get(comment.postId);\n  const parent = comment.parentId ? parentMap.get(comment.parentId) : null;\n  // ...\n}\n```\n\nSame pattern applies to:\n- **Post handler** (line 73–76): batch-fetch groups by `groupId`\n- **PostReaction handler** (lines 149–176): batch-fetch posts, then batch-check existing notifications\n- **CommentReaction handler** (lines 194–197): batch-fetch comments\n- **GroupMember handler** (lines 243–287): batch-fetch groups + admins; 4 separate N+1s in one loop\n- **EventAttendee handler** (lines 392–414): batch-fetch events\n\n---\n\n**`conversationMemberIds` called per message — no caching**\n\n`apps/api/src/server/plugins/realtime-plugin.ts:296, 325, 337, 346`\n```typescript\n// ❌ Same conversation queried on every message in a batch\nfor (const message of rows) {\n  emitToUsers(await conversationMemberIds(message.conversationId), ...);\n}\n\n// ✅ Request-scoped cache (add to realtime-plugin scope)\nconst memberCache = new Map<string, string[]>();\nasync function cachedConversationMembers(id: string) {\n  if (!memberCache.has(id)) {\n    memberCache.set(id, await conversationMemberIds(id));\n  }\n  return memberCache.get(id)!;\n}\n// Clear after the handler batch completes\n```\n\n---\n\n**`callTitle()` called twice per join flow**\n\n`apps/api/src/websocket/calls.ts:231, 287`\n```typescript\n// ❌ Fetches conversation members twice (full objects, not just names)\nconst title = await callTitle(call);  // line 231\n// ... later in same handler ...\nconst title2 = await callTitle(call); // line 287\n\n// ✅ Fetch once, pass as argument; narrow the select to only name fields\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Unnecessary Re-renders\n\n**`message-list.tsx` — `actions` object spread on every render**\n\n`apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx:236`\n```tsx\n// ❌ New object identity on every render → MessageRow always re-renders\n<MessageRow actions={{ ...actions, onJumpTo: jumpTo }} />\n\n// ✅ Memoize stable references\nconst jumpTo = useCallback((id: string) => {\n  if (!messages.some(m => m.id === id)) { toast(...); return; }\n  scrollToMessage(id, { align: \"center\", behavior: \"smooth\" });\n  setHighlight(id);\n}, [messages, scrollToMessage]);\n\nconst mergedActions = useMemo(() => ({ ...actions, onJumpTo: jumpTo }), [actions, jumpTo]);\n\n// Then wrap the component:\nconst MessageRow = React.memo(function MessageRow({ ... }) { ... });\n```\n\n---\n\n**`post-feed.tsx` — inline objects in query args and IntersectionObserver**\n\n`apps/web/src/components/feed/post-feed.tsx:39–68`\n```tsx\n// ❌ New where object on every render → query refetch thrash\nuseDbInfinite(\n  [\"post\", \"findMany\", \"feed\", ...scope],\n  (cursor) => findPosts(me.id, {\n    where: pinnedFirst ? { AND: [where, { pinnedAt: null }] } : where,\n    ...\n  }),\n  PAGE_SIZE\n)\n\n// ✅ Stable query argument\nconst queryWhere = useMemo(\n  () => pinnedFirst ? { AND: [where, { pinnedAt: null }] } : where,\n  [pinnedFirst, where]\n);\n\n// ❌ Options object is a new identity on every effect run\nconst observer = new IntersectionObserver(fn, { rootMargin: \"600px 0px\" });\n\n// ✅ Move outside component or useMemo\nconst OBSERVER_OPTIONS = { rootMargin: \"600px 0px\" };\n```\n\n---\n\n**`post-feed.tsx` — `posts` array rebuilt every render**\n\n`apps/web/src/components/feed/post-feed.tsx:93–96`\n```tsx\n// ❌ Flat + spread on every render\nconst posts = [...(pinnedFirst ? pinned.data ?? [] : []), ...data.pages.flat()];\n\n// ✅\nconst posts = useMemo(\n  () => [...(pinnedFirst ? pinned.data ?? [] : []), ...data.pages.flat()],\n  [pinnedFirst, pinned.data, data.pages]\n);\n```\n\n---\n\n**`contacts-rail.tsx` — sort on every render**\n\n`apps/web/src/components/layout/contacts-rail.tsx:26–28`\n```tsx\n// ❌\nconst sorted = [...people].sort((a, b) => Number(online.has(b.id)) - Number(online.has(a.id)));\n\n// ✅\nconst sorted = useMemo(\n  () => [...people].sort((a, b) => Number(online.has(b.id)) - Number(online.has(a.id))),\n  [people, online]\n);\n```\n\n---\n\n**`message-list.tsx` — array reverse every render**\n\n`apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx:81`\n```tsx\n// ❌\nconst messages = data.pages.flat().reverse();\n\n// ✅\nconst messages = useMemo(() => data.pages.flat().reverse(), [data.pages]);\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Caching Opportunities\n\n| Opportunity | Location | Approach |\n|---|---|---|\n| `conversationMemberIds` | `realtime-plugin.ts` | Request-scoped `Map` cache (see above) |\n| `mentionedReaders()` | `realtime-plugin.ts:78, 122` | Cache by `groupId` within handler batch |\n| Group lookups in all handlers | `realtime-plugin.ts` | Batch-fetch by ID set before loops |\n| `callTitle` | `calls.ts:231, 287` | Fetch once, pass result |\n| TanStack Query stale time | `apps/web/src/lib/query.ts` | Add `staleTime: 30_000` for stable resources (org members, groups) to prevent waterfalls on navigation |\n\n---\n\n### 4. Memory Leaks\n\n**`call-session.ts` — `track.ended` listeners never removed**\n\n`apps/web/src/lib/rtc/call-session.ts:463–469, 477–483, 578–580`\n```typescript\n// ❌ New listener added each time track is replaced; old one stays\ntrack.addEventListener(\"ended\", () => {\n  if (this.audioTrack !== track) return;\n  this.audioTrack = null;\n});\n\n// ✅ Store listener reference and remove before adding new one\nprivate audioTrackEndedListener: (() => void) | null = null;\n\nsetAudioTrack(track: MediaStreamTrack | null) {\n  if (this.audioTrack && this.audioTrackEndedListener) {\n    this.audioTrack.removeEventListener(\"ended\", this.audioTrackEndedListener);\n  }\n  this.audioTrack = track;\n  if (track) {\n    this.audioTrackEndedListener = () => { this.audioTrack = null; /* cleanup */ };\n    track.addEventListener(\"ended\", this.audioTrackEndedListener);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nApply the same pattern to `setCameraTrack` and `toggleScreen`.\n\n---\n\n**`message-list.tsx` — window event listeners accumulate**\n\n`apps/web/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx:263–274`\n\nThe cleanup is correct (empty dep array, removed on unmount), but `update` is recreated on render while listeners hold the initial reference. The current code is safe — no actual leak — but document the intent with a comment, or hoist `update` to a `useCallback` to make it explicitly stable.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Redundant Computations\n\n**`post-card.tsx` — `reactions` filtered without memoization**\n\n`apps/web/src/components/feed/post-card.tsx:79–80`\n```tsx\n// ❌ Recomputed every render\nconst reactions = withOptimistic(post.reactions, me, pendingReaction);\nconst myReaction = reactions.find(r => r.userId === me.id)?.type ?? null;\n\n// ✅\nconst reactions = useMemo(\n  () => withOptimistic(post.reactions, me, pendingReaction),\n  [post.reactions, me, pendingReaction]\n);\nconst myReaction = useMemo(\n  () => reactions.find(r => r.userId === me.id)?.type ?? null,\n  [reactions, me.id]\n);\n```\n\n---\n\n### Priority Order\n\n| Priority | Fix | Impact |\n|---|---|---|\n| **P0** | `notify()` → `createManyAndReturn()` | Immediate DB write reduction |\n| **P0** | Batch-fetch in realtime-plugin handlers (post, comment, reaction, groupMember loops) | Eliminates most N+1s |\n| **P1** | Request-scoped cache for `conversationMemberIds` | Cuts chat message handler DB calls by ~90% |\n| **P1** | `callTitle` fetch once, remove duplicate call | Halves WebRTC join queries |\n| **P2** | `useMemo` on `messages`, `posts`, `sorted`, `reactions` | Fixes render churn in high-frequency components |\n| **P2** | `React.memo` + `useCallback` on `MessageRow` + `jumpTo` | Prevents full chat list re-render on every keystroke |\n| **P2** | Track `ended` listener cleanup in `call-session.ts` | Prevents MediaStreamTrack leak during calls |\n| **P3** | Stable query args in `post-feed.tsx` | Stops unnecessary TanStack Query refetches |\n",
